{
  "$comment": "Inputs of pnpm build:ascii-header (scripts/build/ascii-header.mjs), which writes the dot-matrix header to public/marks/ascii. Every length is in dots, one dot a cell of the grid. The layout is measured from the terminal header Kevin sent on 2026-11-25 (a 10.82 px pitch at its capture size): the globe 32 dots across, the name's cap height 12 dots, its two baselines 16 dots apart and centred on the globe, and 6 empty columns between the globe and the name. mark.threshold is the share of a cell's samples that must fall inside the globe for the cell to take a dot. name.spread thickens the letters across only, by that much of a dot each side, so Katagami Text's verticals (1.5 dots at this size) land on 2 dots and its horizontals stay 1 dot, as the reference draws them. A cell samples a samples by samples grid. dot is the dot's diameter as a share of the pitch. png.pitch is the pitch of the PNG renders in pixels. reference holds the reference's dot grid from its first globe column and its first globe row ('#' a dot), for the agreement the script prints.",
  "margin": 3,
  "samples": 8,
  "dot": 0.64,
  "mark": {
    "size": 32,
    "threshold": 0.5
  },
